# sysutils_sysctl (Data Source)

{{ .Description | trimspace }}

The data source validates keys, reads `/proc/sys` and parses sysctl configuration files with the same code as the [`sysutils_sysctl`](../resources/sysctl.md) resource, so `value` and `persisted_value` are normalized the same way as the resource's `value`. It has two modes:

| Mode | Set | Attributes filled in |
|------|-----|----------------------|
| One parameter | `name` | `exists`, `value`, `persisted_value`, `persisted_file` |
| A group of parameters | `prefix` | `values`, `persisted_values` |

A parameter the kernel does not have is not an error: `exists` is false and `value` is null. Likewise, a prefix that does not exist yields an empty `values` map.

