## Which files are read

`persisted_value`, `persisted_file` and `persisted_values` describe what `systemd-sysctl` and `sysctl --system` apply at boot:

1. The `*.conf` files of `/etc/sysctl.d`, `/run/sysctl.d`, `/usr/local/lib/sysctl.d`, `/usr/lib/sysctl.d` and `/lib/sysctl.d`. Of several files with the same name, only the one in the earliest directory counts, so `/etc/sysctl.d/10-foo.conf` hides `/usr/lib/sysctl.d/10-foo.conf`. A file that is a symlink to `/dev/null` sets nothing and still hides files of the same name. Hidden files are ignored.
2. These files are applied sorted by name, whatever directory they are in.
3. `/etc/sysctl.conf` is applied last.

The last assignment of a key wins. Keys in the slash-separated form, such as `net/ipv4/ip_forward`, are converted to the dotted form, and a leading `-` (ignore errors) is dropped. `persisted_file` is the path of the file as listed above, even if it is a symlink, such as Debian's `/etc/sysctl.d/99-sysctl.conf`.

Files that `sysutils_sysctl` writes to its default location, `/etc/sysctl.d/99-terraform.conf`, are included. A `file` of `sysutils_sysctl` outside these directories is not.

## With `root_dir`

With the provider's `root_dir` set, the configuration files are read below `root_dir`, following symlinks inside the tree, and `persisted_*` describe the image being built. The running kernel is not part of that image, so `exists`, `value` and `values` are null.

## Errors

| Situation | Diagnostic |
|-----------|------------|
| Both or neither of `name` and `prefix` are set | `Invalid Attribute Combination` |
| `name` is a group of parameters, such as `net.ipv4.conf.all` | `Reading kernel parameter` (use `prefix`) |
| `name` cannot be read, for example because it is write-only | `Reading kernel parameter` |
| A configuration file cannot be read, is larger than 4 MiB, or is a symlink that leads above `root_dir` | `Reading sysctl configuration` |

## Caveats

- Parameters are those of the provider's namespaces: in a container, the `net.*` parameters are those of the container's network namespace.
- Glob patterns in configuration keys, such as `net.ipv4.conf.*.rp_filter`, are not expanded. They appear in `persisted_values` as written, but never in `persisted_value`.
- `values` leaves out parameters that cannot be read, such as `vm.compact_memory`, which is write-only, and `net.ipv6.conf.*.stable_secret` while it is unset.
- It is read during planning. A value that a `sysutils_sysctl` resource in the same configuration sets is only seen if the data source depends on that resource.
